(LST-54 — WITHDRAWN, 2026-08-29 (0.4.15, #111). HISTORICAL, 0.4.14 and
 earlier: on those manuals, a self-referential map printed 64 levels
 deep, then `...`, set the error flag, and unwound safely.

 As of 0.4.15, `set loopy's "self" to loopy.` copies loopy's state at
 the moment of the `set` (before "self" exists), so this program now
 prints `{"tag": 1, "self": {"tag": 1}}` — one level deep, no error, no
 handler firing. See LST-82 for the direct 0.4.15 probe (`LST-82.vox`)
 and LANGUAGE.md:2593-2597 for the citation. Retained as the historical
 record of the pre-#111 behavior.
